# Mem0 auto-write (mandatory)

**Global rule** — `~/.cursor/rules/` via `python brain.py onboard`. Also injected on sessionStart and in MCP server instructions.

When **AutoLinkingBrain** MCP is available, persist knowledge **in the same session** you learn it.

## When to call storeKnowledge

| Trigger | scenario | Example |
|---------|----------|---------|
| Chose architecture / pattern | architecture | "Auth uses JWT in middleware X" |
| Fixed non-trivial bug | bugfix | root cause + fix location |
| Changed or added API | api_contract | endpoint, DTO, breaking change |
| Completed reindex slice | indexing | module map, entrypoints |
| Learned project-specific gotcha | architecture | env, deploy, config trap |
| Finished ArchitectureCurator feature slice | architecture | summary + `docs/ARCHITECTURE.generated.md` path |
| Hard debugging / non-obvious root cause | bugfix | symptoms, cause, fix — `scope: both` if reusable |
| Cross-project pattern (ES, SQL, JVM, caching, etc.) | architecture | `scope: global` or `both` — write **expanded** (constraints → what worked) |

One fact per call. **Project-local:** include a **file path** in `text` or `context_path`. **Global patterns:** path optional; prefer concrete rules (settings, query shape, index mapping).

## global_skills (`scope: global` | `both`)

- **`global`** — transferable know-how (Elasticsearch indexing conventions, DB query plans, lock contention, framework traps) without tying to one repo.
- **`both`** — same pattern **plus** how it applies in the current project (keep one dense fact, not two vague ones).
- **`project`** (default) — only this codebase (module map, local API, deploy).

Hooks **autolog** → **SQLite** `.cursor/autolog.db` only (not Mem0 unless `MEM0_AUTOLOG_ALLOW_MEM0=1`). Read logs with **`listSessionAutolog`** / **`searchSessionAutolog`**. Curated recall = **`storeKnowledge`** only.

Body may be long (up to ~5500 chars) — use for “lessons learned”, not one-liners.

**Generated arch MD alone is not enough** — after each module `recordAgentArchitectureReview` → `storeKnowledge` (scenario: architecture, paths to `docs/architecture/modules/<slug>.md`).

## Minimum per session

- **Start:** `checkProjectHealth` (or `sessionContextPack` once).
- **During:** ≥1 `storeKnowledge` if you made any decision or discovery worth recalling.
- **End of task:** if nothing stored yet but work was done → one summary `storeKnowledge`.

## MCP call pattern

```
server: user-AutoLinkingBrain
tool: storeKnowledge
{ text: "English fact with path src/foo.py ...", tech: "...", scenario: "architecture", scope: "project", context_path: "..." }

# Global pattern example:
{ text: "Elasticsearch: use nested for X; avoid scripting on Y; reindex alias Z …", tech: "elasticsearch", scenario: "architecture", scope: "global" }
```

If MCP errors: note briefly, continue work — retry store on next stable turn.
